# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything personal stays on this machine. This repo is pushed to GitHub, so
# nothing identifying may be tracked — not the signature, not the photo, not the
# address, not the application history. A pushed signature cannot be recalled.
# The local-only backup repo (tools/backup_local.sh) versions these instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Contact details + the forbidden-claim rules
identity.local.json

# The profile vault: home address, phone, full biography
my_profile/

# CV and cover-letter masters: embed the profile photo and handwritten signature
# as base64 data URIs, plus the home address. The *_example.html files are tracked
# on purpose - they carry the anchors tools/make_app.py needs, with placeholder
# art and no real person's details, so a fresh clone is actually runnable.
templates/**
!templates/cv_example.html
!templates/cover_example.html

# Application history: every employer applied to, with notes on stated weaknesses
tracker.csv

# Drafted queues: the exact documents prepared, and the ranked weak points
applications/**
!applications/.gitkeep

# Retired ai-job-search output
archive/

# Diplomas, transcripts, reference letters - and both derived files. EXTRACT.md is
# the raw pull from them; EVIDENCE.md is the agent's reading of it. A transcript and a
# reference letter are more personal than anything else in this repo.
documents/**
!documents/README.md

# One-off scripts from individual runs: they carry that run's data inline
tools/_*.py

# Search queries: they describe one person's target market and role type
queries.txt
!queries.example.txt

# Scrape state: regenerable, and a record of what has been shown
seen.json
latest.json
ranked.json
ranked.template.json

# The judging bundle: every new posting's full text, fetched fresh each run
to_judge.md

# Build artifacts
*.pdf
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.venv/
